 "publish": {
  "youtube_titles": [
   "Why Smart People Overthink—and How to Stop It",
   "The Hidden Cost of Overthinking: A Real‑Life Story",
   "From Endless Rehearsal to Real Action: Alex’s Journey"
  ],
  "description": "In this animated essay we follow Alex as he wrestles with the habit of overthinking. Through everyday scenes—typing drafts, scrolling reports, and a candid coffee‑shop chat—we see the difference between gathering new information and rehearsing the same imagined outcomes. The film shows how recognizing the loop can free us to act, even on decisions that feel high‑stakes.\n\nThe story also addresses the common objection that important, hard‑to‑reverse choices deserve deep scrutiny. By contrasting thoughtful research with endless mental rehearsal, Alex learns to communicate honest uncertainty and move forward without spiraling. #Overthinking #DecisionMaking #MentalHealth #Productivity #AnimatedEssay\n",
  "tags": [
   "overthinking",
   "rumination",
   "decision making",
